{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>To satisfy your hunger.</b> There is a hint in his language that it is not fitting for a person to pursue the desires of food and drink, but only for the sustaining of the body alone, to satisfy his hunger, as it is written (Proverbs 13:25): ״צדיק אוכל לשובע נפשו״. And therefore he used the expression 'to satisfy your hunger' even though it was in the days of the famine. And know that the essence of the fear of HaShem is separation from the desires of the world, and from this he began and said, ״את האלהים אני ירא״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:49.076011224Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}